From: Kholin <oodzchen@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x: report and switch SoundWire channels individually

The "ADCn Switch" style controls add or remove one channel of a codec
SoundWire port, but their get handler reports the port: all four ADC
switches of the TX device read 1 as soon as one of them is on, because
ADC1-ADC4 share WCD939X_ADC_1_4_PORT. Saving the mixer state (alsactl
store at shutdown) therefore records ADC2 and ADC3 as on, and restoring
it at the next boot sets their channel bits. With only ADC1 and ADC4
routed (the OnePlus Pad 2 Pro microphones), the codec then transmits a
four-channel port (mask 0xf, or 0x6 in another boot) while the SoC side
expects two, and capture returns full-scale noise; whether a boot works
depends on the mixer state it restored. The put handler also always
returned 1.

Report the channel's own bit in the port's channel mask, keep
port_enable as "any channel of the port is on", and return whether the
mask changed.

Seen on OPD2413 (SM8750, WCD9395): the codec port 1 channel-enable
register read 0xf with ADC2/ADC3 restored on; after turning them off it
read 0x9 and the microphones recorded normally.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c | 20 ++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
index 80f3e7276..559424388 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -2053,7 +2053,13 @@ static int wcd939x_get_swr_port(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 	}
 	portidx = wcd->ch_info[ch_id].port_num;
 
-	ucontrol->value.integer.value[0] = wcd->port_enable[portidx] ? 1 : 0;
+	/*
+	 * Several channels share one port (ADC1-4 on the TX device): report
+	 * this channel, not the port, so that saving and restoring the mixer
+	 * state cannot turn on channels nobody asked for.
+	 */
+	ucontrol->value.integer.value[0] =
+		!!(wcd->port_config[portidx - 1].ch_mask & wcd->ch_info[ch_id].ch_mask);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -2079,7 +2085,8 @@ static int wcd939x_set_swr_port(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 	struct wcd939x_priv *wcd939x = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(comp);
 	struct wcd939x_sdw_priv *wcd = wcd939x->sdw_priv[mixer->shift];
 	unsigned int ch_id = mixer->reg;
-	unsigned int portidx;
+	unsigned int portidx, old_mask;
+	bool enable;
 
 	/* in HPH PCM mode the HPH stream rides the HIFI_PCM port */
 	if (wcd939x->hph_pcm_enabled && !wcd->is_tx) {
@@ -2089,12 +2096,13 @@ static int wcd939x_set_swr_port(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 			ch_id = WCD939X_HIFI_PCM_R;
 	}
 	portidx = wcd->ch_info[ch_id].port_num;
+	enable = !!ucontrol->value.integer.value[0];
+	old_mask = wcd->port_config[portidx - 1].ch_mask;
 
-	wcd->port_enable[portidx] = !!ucontrol->value.integer.value[0];
+	wcd939x_connect_port(wcd, portidx, ch_id, enable);
+	wcd->port_enable[portidx] = !!wcd->port_config[portidx - 1].ch_mask;
 
-	wcd939x_connect_port(wcd, portidx, ch_id, wcd->port_enable[portidx]);
-
-	return 1;
+	return wcd->port_config[portidx - 1].ch_mask != old_mask;
 }
 
 /* MBHC Related */
